<title>USA: Intermet sees Q4 results hurt by GM strike.</title>
<headline>Intermet sees Q4 results hurt by GM strike.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermet Corp said Thursday a strike against General Motors Corp's Canadian operations would hurt the auto parts supplier's fourth-quarter results.</p>
<p>The extent of the damage depends on the length of the strike, which is now two weeks old, Intermet said.</p>
<p>&quot;If all GM-related sales stop, the cost to Intermet will probably be in the range of $0.03 to $0.04 earnings per share for each month of stoppage,&quot; said John Doddridge, the company's chairman, in a statement accompanying its third-quarter results.</p>
</text>
